From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:43:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] socket: queue a burst of host-forward connections

tcpx_listen() listened with a backlog of one. libslirp accepts one
connection per poll pass, so the host kernel has to queue the rest of a
burst of connects on the forward's listening socket, and a queue of one
refuses or resets them before libslirp sees them. On macOS, 32
simultaneous loopback connects to one forward got 10 to 15 through.

Listen with SOMAXCONN, the host's own limit for a listening queue
(128 on macOS). Upstream master still listens with a backlog of one.
---
 src/socket.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/socket.c b/src/socket.c
index fa48cdaa8f0803fc099a536ba85a486f3165f196..6b65be197eea31e8bcb4ce22b1c29327a11198de 100644
--- a/src/socket.c
+++ b/src/socket.c
@@ -876,7 +876,12 @@ struct socket *tcpx_listen(Slirp *slirp,
         (haddr->sa_family == AF_INET6 && slirp_socket_set_v6only(s, (flags & SS_HOSTFWD_V6ONLY) != 0) < 0) ||
         (slirp_socket_set_fast_reuse(s) < 0) ||
         (bind(s, haddr, haddrlen) < 0) ||
-        (listen(s, 1) < 0)) {
+        /*
+         * One connection is accepted per poll pass, so the host kernel
+         * queues the rest of a burst of connects; a shorter queue than the
+         * burst refuses or resets the overflow before we see it.
+         */
+        (listen(s, SOMAXCONN) < 0)) {
         int tmperrno = errno; /* Don't clobber the real reason we failed */
         if (have_valid_socket(s)) {
             closesocket(s);
